{"edits": [{"finding_ids": ["scripts/clean_backup.py:146:deprecated-method", "scripts/clean_backup.py:147:deprecated-method"], "search": "            User.parse_obj({"user_id": args.user_id, "user_type": args.user_type}),
            User.parse_obj(
                {
                    "user_id": args.replacement_user_id,
                    "user_type": args.replacement_user_type,
                }
            ),", "replace": "            User.model_validate({"user_id": args.user_id, "user_type": args.user_type}),
            User.model_validate(
                {
                    "user_id": args.replacement_user_id,
                    "user_type": args.replacement_user_type,
                }
            ),", "explanation": "Pydantic v2 deprecates BaseModel.parse_obj() in favor of model_validate(), per the migration guide table (parse_obj() -> model_validate()). Both User.parse_obj calls in the replace-user branch are replaced in a single edit covering the contiguous lines 146-154, so the edits do not overlap. The dict arguments and behavior are unchanged. The existing `from models import User, UserType` import is still needed, so no import changes are required."}], "notes": "Both findings (lines 146 and 147) are the same deprecated `User.parse_obj(...)` -> `User.model_validate(...)` change, and they sit in one contiguous block. I combined them into a single edit so the search string is unique and nothing overlaps. `User` is a Pydantic model per the findings, and `model_validate` accepts the same dict input, so behavior is preserved. No other edits are needed. `replace_user` mutates plain dict/list permission data and the `User` attributes, which is not a v1 API. `User` and `UserType` are still used, so the import stays as is."}
